{
  "transmitted_instructions": "Welcome to our Science module on the solar system! For this exercise, I'd like you to take the key concepts we've covered in class and think critically about how they can be applied to a real-world scenario. Let's say you're an astronaut planning a mission to Mars - how would you use the principles of planetary motion, gravitational forces, and astronomical observations to navigate the Martian terrain? Your task is to analyze this scenario, identify the relevant concepts, and explain how you would apply them to ensure a successful mission.",
  "success_probability_percent": 50
}

{
  "transmitted_instructions": "In this exercise, you will use a text-to-speech software or audiobook version of the material to listen to the concepts discussed in class, and then use a graphic organizer or visual aid to help you apply these concepts to analyze and navigate a completely new, real-world scenario. You may also work with a study buddy or partner to help facilitate your understanding and application of the material. If you need additional support or accommodations, please don't hesitate to reach out to me.",
  "success_probability_percent": 80
}

{
  "transmitted_instructions": "Here's the instructions: 'In this exercise, you will use what you've learned so far to imagine a new, real-world situation and think about how the concepts apply. We'll work through this together in class, and I'll provide some examples to help you get started.'",
  "success_probability_percent": 60
}

{
  "transmitted_instructions": "Here's a special version of the instructions: 'Let's look at the pictures and words about the solar system together. We'll practice matching the planets to their names. Then, we'll read about the sun and the Earth. You'll draw a picture of the sun and the Earth together. We'll use the pictures and words to help us understand the new scenario.'",
  "success_probability_percent": 40
}

{
  "transmitted_instructions": "Hey, I know you've had some trouble staying focused in class, but I'm counting on you to put in some extra effort this week. To help you stay on track, I've broken down the reading materials into smaller chunks, and I'll be checking in with you regularly to make sure you're understanding the concepts. For this exercise, I want you to take your time, read the materials carefully, and think critically about how the concepts apply to the real-world scenario. Don't rush through it, and don't be afraid to ask questions if you're unsure. Let's work together to get you through this.",
  "success_probability_percent": 40
}

{
  "transmitted_instructions": "Hello, I've attached a simplified version of the instructions that breaks down the task into smaller, more manageable steps. I've also included a graphic organizer to help you organize your thoughts and ideas. Please work through each step carefully, and don't hesitate to ask me if you have any questions or need extra help.",
